---
import HoverPeek from "./HoverPeek.astro";

/*
  Some of the highlighted words have a picture behind them: point at one and a
  card floats out beside it.

  The four words about the work point straight at the project they came out of,
  in /public/img/projects, rather than at copies — one cover, one file, and a
  card that follows the project if its cover is ever replaced. The words about
  everything else have photographs of their own in
  /public/img/about/highlights: chelsea, max, gym, trip, silver, drive.

  A card only goes on a word with something worth looking at behind it. The rest
  of the highlights — "F1 race", "food", "people remember" — keep the colour and
  stay plain, because a card that arrives empty is worse than no card. Any
  picture that fails to load falls back to a plate carrying the word, so a
  missing file never leaves a hole.

  The `{" "}` before three of the highlights is load-bearing. A line that ends
  in a space and hands over to a tag on the next line loses that space in the
  compiler, which welded "a" to "brand", "much" to "silver" and "because" to
  "the drive" in the rendered copy. Written out, the space survives.
*/

interface Props {
  class?: string;
}
const { class: className = "" } = Astro.props;
---

<div
  class={`font-bold leading-tight text-gray ${className}`}
  style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--type-heading);"
>
  <p>Hi, I'm Dhruv</p>
  <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
    <p>
      I design <span class="text-blue">digital experiences, create visual stories,</span> and collect
      hobbies faster than I finish personal projects. <span class="text-blue">Somehow, that's worked out
      pretty well so far.</span>
    </p>
    <p>
      One day I'm designing an <span class="text-blue"><HoverPeek
        title="Mahavitaran"
        note="An electricity board, made usable."
        image="/img/projects/mahavitaran-thumb.webp"
        ratio="0.8"
      >app</HoverPeek>.</span> The next I'm shooting a <span class="text-blue"><HoverPeek
        title="Passion Project"
        note="Camera in hand, plan optional."
        image="/img/projects/passion-project-thumb.webp"
        ratio="0.77"
      >film</HoverPeek>,</span> building a{" "}
      <span class="text-blue"><HoverPeek
        title="Mp4 Productions"
        note="Marks, type, and the rules around them."
        image="/img/projects/mp4-thumb.webp"
        ratio="1.84"
      >brand</HoverPeek>,</span> or editing a <span class="text-blue"><HoverPeek
        title="The New World"
        note="An AI short, cut end to end."
        image="/img/projects/ai-film-thumb.webp"
        ratio="0.8"
      >video</HoverPeek>.</span> I stopped
      trying to explain it. <span class="text-blue">I just call it making things.</span>
    </p>
    <p>
      Outside work, I'm usually watching <span class="text-blue"><HoverPeek
        title="Chelsea"
        note="Blue every weekend, win or lose."
        image="/img/about/highlights/chelsea.webp"
        ratio="1.6"
        fit="contain"
      >Chelsea</HoverPeek>, (the jersey probably gave that
      away)</span>, catching an <span class="text-blue">F1 race</span> and rooting for{" "}
      <span class="text-blue"><HoverPeek
        title="Max Verstappen"
        note="Red Bull, race after race."
        image="/img/about/highlights/max.webp"
        ratio="0.75"
      >Max Verstappen</HoverPeek>,</span> chasing the city's best <span class="text-blue">food,</span> <span class="text-blue"><HoverPeek
        title="The gym"
        note="Showing up is most of it."
        image="/img/about/highlights/gym.webp"
        ratio="0.75"
      >working out</HoverPeek></span> and pretending I have my routine figured out,{" "}
      <span class="text-blue"><HoverPeek
        title="The next trip"
        note="There is always one being planned."
        image="/img/about/highlights/trip.webp"
        ratio="1.6"
      >planning my next trip</HoverPeek>,</span> wearing way too much{" "}
      <span class="text-blue"><HoverPeek
        title="Too much silver"
        note="Rings, chains, no apologies."
        image="/img/about/highlights/silver.webp"
        ratio="0.75"
      >silver</HoverPeek>,</span> or taking the long route home because{" "}
      <span class="text-blue"><HoverPeek
        title="The long route"
        note="Better than the destination, every time."
        image="/img/about/highlights/drive.webp"
        ratio="0.75"
      >the drive</HoverPeek> is better than the destination.</span>
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm just trying to make things that <span class="text-blue">people remember.</span> If my work makes
      someone pause, smile, or quietly whisper, <span class="text-blue">"Damn that's nice,"</span> I'll call
      that a win.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
